Title: "An Example"
Id: "0f26c41e-8056-43dd-9762-675a96f8618f"

Text: "A small definition can combine prose, a command header, type requirements, rendering metadata, and an automatically generated ID.

```mlg-fragment
Text: \"A subset is a set whose elements all belong to another set.\"

[A \:subset:/ B]
Declares: A
when: B is \set
extends: A is \set
satisfies:
. forAll: X \"in\" A
  then: X \"in\"? B
Documented:
. written: \"A? \subseteq B?\"
. called: \"$A?$ is a subset of $B?$\"
Id: \"4196f823-e51d-4568-89aa-83a2d4627bd9\"
```

The command header introduces the notation. `Declares:` makes the construct a
reusable type-like specification. The `when:` section says what the header
parameter `B` must satisfy. The `extends:` section lets the checker use a subset
as a set. The `satisfies:` section records the defining condition. `called:` and
`written:` tell `mlg view` how to render the item in prose and math contexts."
Id: "44c3ad88-6c51-45f0-acd0-55148245fede"
